meta {
    title: "DocUP: Full Feature Test",
    author: "Prathmesh",
    version: "1.0.0"
}

h(1) { DocUP Phase 1 }

h(2, id: "intro", class: "section") { Introduction }

p {
    DocUP is a document markup language with b{single-pass parsing}, i{zero
    ambiguity}, and explicit scoping. This paragraph shows b{bold}, i{italic},
    b{i{bold italic}}, strike{strikethrough}, and inline code{let x = 1;} all in
    one place.
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "links") { Links and Quotes }

p {
    Learn more at link("https://example.com"){the DocUP homepage}, or read the
    link("https://example.com/spec"){language spec}.
}

quote {
    Good design is as little design as possible.

    quote { A nested quote, for attributing a quote within a quote. }
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "lists") { Lists }

p { An unordered list of core features, with a nested sub-list: }

list {
    item {
        Metadata blocks for document info

        list(ordered: true) {
            item { Nested ordered child A }
            item { Nested ordered child B }
        }
    }
    item { Headings from h(1) through h(6) }
    item { Paragraphs with b{bold}, i{italic}, and code{inline code} }
}

p { An ordered list of build steps: }

list(ordered: true) {
    item { Lex the source into tokens }
    item { Parse tokens into an AST }
    item { Analyze the AST for errors }
    item { Generate the final HTML }
}

p { A task list of project milestones: }

list {
    task(done: true) { Design the grammar }
    task(done: true) { Write the parser }
    task(done: false) { Reach v0.3.1 }
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "media") { Images and Code }

image("https://example.com/diagram.png", alt: "Architecture diagram")

codeblock(lang: "go", file: "main.go") {!
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Closing brace } and quotes \" work fine!")
}
!}

hr {}

h(2, id: "table") { Tables }

table {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { Feature }
        cell { Status }
    }
    row {
        cell { Tables }
        cell { b{Done} }
    }
    row {
        cell { Nested lists and quotes }
        cell { b{Done} }
    }
}

p {
    That's all 15 features: meta, headings, paragraphs, inline styling (bold,
    italic, code, strikethrough), codeblock, hr, list/item, link, quote, image,
    nested lists, nested quotes, task lists, and tables.
}
